-- title:
--   Centred Igusa datum: jmatĥ or jmatĥ⁻¹ regular (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$, a level $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$; let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Further data: a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in that reduced field, compatible coefficientwise with reduction of Laurent series over $A$ (hypothesis $hR_0$); an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the explicit description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as the quotients of coefficientwise images of Laurent series over $A$ with denominator of nonzero reduction, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-translates $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ on the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, permutation of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ by all level automorphisms, the contraction $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)\cap\overline{\mathbb Q}=A$, the statement that $R_0$-integral elements regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is and whose residue is $s$-integral lie in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with the expected centre, invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under the level automorphisms, and the existence in each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ of an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$; a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image is $A\cap K_0$, with surjective induced residue map, and with a generator $\varpi_0$ of its maximal ideal satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; the subfield $F_0\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of $jq$, with the $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ induced by $\iota$. Finally fix a line $\ell$, a valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ contained in (and strictly smaller than) the trace of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ on $F_0$, an $A_0$-subalgebra $B\subseteq F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$, subject to: $B$ finitely generated, integrally closed in $F_0$ with fraction field $F_0$, every non-maximal prime containing $\varpi_0 B$ minimal over it, every nonzero prime not containing $\varpi_0 B$ having a valuation-subring localisation, $\ell$ the only line whose Igusa ring contains $B$, no $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ containing $B$, $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)\cap F_0$ a localisation of $B$ at some prime and also at every minimal prime over $\varpi_0B$, $B\subseteq V$, and $\mathfrak m$ the preimage of the nonunits of $V$; and assume some $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$-translate $x$ of $\hat\jmath$ (by an element of the subgroup generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) satisfies $x\in B$ or $x^{-1}\in B$. The conclusion is that $\hat\jmath$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1}$ lies in the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m$: there are $b,c\in B$ with $c\notin\mathfrak m$ and $\hat\jmath\,c=b$, or there are such $b,c$ with $\hat\jmath^{-1}c=b$.
--
--   This is a local regularity step on the Igusa-chart leg of the construction of a semistable covering of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over a valuation ring above $q$: at a datum $(B,\mathfrak m)$ centring a proper refinement of the Igusa valuation ring at the line $\ell$, the modular invariant or its inverse is shown to be regular at the centre. It is the case $q=3$, and it feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_forall_gaussBranch_descent_local_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_forall_gaussBranch_descent_local_of_eq_three).
